    "subjectCode": "SSC102",
    "syllabusName": "Business Communication_Kỹ năng giao tiếp",
    "syllabusEnglish": null,
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": "Bachelor in Business Administration",
    "timeAllocation": "Study hour (150h) = 45 contact hours (60 sessions) + 1 hour final exam + 104 hours self-study",
    "prerequisite": "ENT503 or equivalent English qualification.",
    "description": "The course stresses a balanced approach to communication by in written and oral essential form of business communication. It is also to give the learners opportunities to practice face to face communication, listening and non-verbal messages, presentation skills, job interview; technology, multicultural and global communication, business ethics and teamwork are integrated in content and applications throughout the course.his course addresses the fundamental elements of communication in business environment to equip learners with essential communication tools to ensure success for both individuals and organization.\n\nUpon the completion of this course, the learners will be able to:\n\n(1) Communication effectively in writting the basic and practical business correspondence including letters, emails, and advanced ones as reports, proposals, business plans…\n\n(2) communicate effectively face-to-face communication as presenting, listening, feedback, nonverbal messages in different business contexts including socialization, staff meetings, meetings with colleagues, customers and partners...\n\n(3) successfully in the job search, résume and interviewing communication including writing application letters, CV, and prepare job interview in variety situations..\n\n(4) personalize their communication style to enhance communicative effects and leave good impresson on readers/audience.",
    "studentTasks": "'- Students must attend more than 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination.\n\n- Student is responsible to do all tasks assigned by instructor in class or at home and submit on time;\n\n- Use laptop in class for learning/exam purposes only;",
